tor that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x, y, z) = (1,-1, 2)$."] [17592186124994 :question/worked-solution "A nonzero gradient is perpendicular to its level surface. Here $$\\nabla f=\\langle y+5,x,2z\\rangle.$$ Evaluating at $(1,-1,2)$ gives $\\langle4,1,4\\rangle=4\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j+4\\mathbf k$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186122357 17592186122358 17592186122359 17592186122360 17592186122361 17592186122987 17592186122988 17592186122989 17592186122990 17592186122991] "immutable_fields" [[17592186122356 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122356 :answer-field/id] [17592186122356 :answer-field/key] [17592186122356 :answer-field/type] [17592186122986 :answer-field/correct] [17592186122986 :answer-field/id] [17592186122986 :answer-field/key] [17592186122986 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
